{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 68, :comments ["<b>In ships.</b> And they will return — children and women — for if they had taken them on foot, only the adults who were able to walk on foot would have returned." "<b>And no one shall buy.</b> R. Joseph explains the verse to mean that the Egyptians will say: Even if you give them to us for free, we will not take them as slaves, because our forefathers were enslaved by them and were stricken with all kinds of plagues. And when the merchants see that they are worth nothing to them, they will beat them with sticks and starve them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:25.080097537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}